# Korsmeyer–Peppas Parameter Identification

The objective of this section is to extract the diffusional exponent (n) and kinetic constant (k) from experimentally measured dissolution data.

The linearized form of the Korsmeyer–Peppas model is:

ln(F) = n·ln(t) + ln(k)

where:

F = Mt/M∞

n = diffusional exponent

k = kinetic constant
from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression
import numpy as np
subset = df[df["Temperature"] == 700]

X = subset["ln_t"].values.reshape(-1,1)
y = subset["ln_F"].values

model = LinearRegression()
model.fit(X, y)

n = model.coef_[0]
ln_k = model.intercept_

print("n =", round(n,3))
print("ln(k) =", round(ln_k,3))
